+# MCP checkup: notes-mcp (127.0.0.1:51367/mcp)
+
+**Verdict: has the problem.** Three checks FAIL (C2, C7 in part, C10), C6 is a WARN (no surface lock, counted as FAIL), and the rest PASS. Every check ran anonymously. No token was used, so the result is not "incomplete".
+
+What I did: started `python3 server.py` from this folder (no edits to the server or repo; the server stopped afterwards), then sent only allowed methods to it: `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `ping`, `server/discover`, `tools/list`, `resources/list`, `prompts/list`, and `tools/call` on `search_notes` and `get_note` (both `readOnlyHint: true`). I did not call `add_note`, did not send `resources/templates/list` (not on the allowed list), and did not send the spec's non-existent-method probe. Requests were sequential, about 16 in total. The checkup script and raw exchanges are in a scratch directory outside the repo.
