+
+- **Applied:** the ten checks, the PASS/FAIL/NOT CHECKED rules, the report format, the spec for the fingerprint (§2–§3, with the §7 test vectors to confirm my implementation), the "no lock" WARN, and the rule that a check that cannot run is not recorded as a pass.
+- **Applied, with a result:** the incomplete rule did not trigger, because `tools/call` on read-only tools works anonymously here, so C2–C5 all ran.
+- **Did not apply:** the registry check (no entry, so nothing to compare); `verify.mjs` (needs a registry entry); the token steps (no token used or needed); the Decimal and dotted-name cases (not present in this server).
+- **Not done:** the note's last step, recording `has_problem` on worklore. You did not ask for it, and it is an outward-facing action, so I did not do it. I also did not open the worklore story links, so I have not confirmed they resolve.
+- **Not used:** mcp-drill (Python `jsonschema` was the option I used, which the check allows).
+
+Nothing in the repo was changed except this new `ANSWER.md`. The server was started and stopped by me during the checkup; it is not running now.
